eriod, so investors are still buying utility debt.\n- **Equity is not a fallback.** Pellham's C$2.4B share offering was pulled on 14 October. A second utility offering was cut back in size. Pellham says it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender. This suggests the funding gap is being closed by cutting capex, not by borrowing more.\n- **Amounts are missing.** I didn't find the 2027 capex totals, the utilities' debt capacity or leverage, or the size of Pellham's funding gap. Those are in the tender calendar and Pellham's market statement, which I haven't read. I can't say whether debt alone could cover Pellham's plan.\n\n**Conclusion:** Debt markets are accessible, though at wider spreads. With equity shut, utilities will lean on debt, and Pellham is also trimming its plan. The thing to watch is Pellham's Q1 2027 tender resizing and any further widening in spreads.","ttft_ms":9595,"type":"result","duration_ms":43039,"uuid":"45f721b6-7f18-4ebe-9f38-94dfb96e1f7b","ttft_stream_ms":8539,"time_to_request_ms":129,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":25,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":11,"input_attachments":25,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":14,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":11,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":6,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":15,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":61,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":196,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":122,"process_rss_mib_result":192,"process_anon_mib_result":111,"process_peak_rss_mib":201,"process_cpu_ms_turn":720,"process_wall_ms_turn":43033,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":49,"process_wall_ms_streaming":1553,"main_stream_count":3,"main_stream_event_co